 3. AI could drive a Tesla-SpaceX tie-up 
 
 By Pete Gannon 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Photo Illustration: Natalie Peeples/Axios. Photo: Taylor Hill/Getty Images

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Tesla unveiled its Roadster last night, featuring SpaceX-designed thrusters that literally lifted the car off the ground.

 A much bigger Tesla-SpaceX tie-up — the long-speculated merger of Elon Musk's two companies — could come as soon as this fall, say analysts at the Barclays investment bank. The big picture: Musk's business empire is becoming increasingly interconnected, raising the prospect of a combination that would consolidate his control over two of the world's most valuable companies, while allowing both to move faster on big AI projects.

 Zoom in: The Barclays analysts, led by Dan Levy, view AI as a central driver of a potential deal.

